# Two-Tier Clean-Room Reverse Engineering Pipeline (morluto/rea + Vertex AI)

## Architectural Principle (DEC-048)

To extract architectural patterns from quarantined foreign repositories (`../DNK_Vibe/`) without contaminating DNK OS production codebases (`apps/`, `core/`, `services/`), assimilation operates across two strictly decoupled tiers:

```
[ Quarantined Codebase in ../DNK_Vibe/<target> ]
                       │
                       ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Tier 1: Local In-RAM Inspection (FastMCP / REABridge)  │
│  • AST extraction & schema deconstruction in memory    │
│  • DOM, CDP, and Wakaru unbundling without live exec   │
│  • Emits: CleanRoomObservation / ArtifactObservation   │
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                           │ Zero source code / Zero contamination
                           ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Tier 2: Google Cloud Vertex AI Sovereign Synthesis     │
│  • REST API: us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com     │
│  • Models: Gemini 4 Argon / Gemini 2.5 Flash / Pro     │
│  • Synthesizes native DNK OS adapters (DNK-STD-0075)   │
│  • Generates deterministic pytest suites (Exit Code 0) │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Physical Components in DNK OS
- `core/cleanroom_re/rea_bridge.py`: Inspects donor sandbox in RAM, recovers module exports, CDP tools, and AST signatures.
- `core/cleanroom_re/vertex_re_synthesizer.py`: Connects CleanRoom observations to Vertex AI endpoint with fallback to deterministic local mock for testing.
- `core/cleanroom_re/schemas.py`: Pydantic contracts for observation interchange.

## Key Invariants
1. **[ZERO_CONTAMINATION]**: Donor code never imported or mounted in production tree.
2. **[TOKEN_BUDGET]**: AST filtered in RAM before LLM dispatch (DEC-044).
3. **[AUTH_REDACTION]**: All Bearer tokens and GCP keys masked in logs.
